title: Payers › List › Search and pick a payer
route: /payers/:id?tab=process
intro: The 'Payers' card: one compact row per payer with its plan type, programs, what it asks for and a mark when a change is waiting, how search narrows the list and what happens when a payer is picked. The tab that was open stays open. Approval rate and decision time are not on this page: Analytics has them.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Look at the 'Payers' card\non the left of the page\n(above the payer on a narrow screen)"
screen list "Payers card\n'Payers' and '3 with a change waiting'\n'Search payers' box, then one row per payer"
process grp "Rows follow the group order\nOhio Medicaid, Commercial,\nMedicare Advantage, Behavioral carve-out\nA payer added later joins its group"
process row "Each row has two lines on the left\nName, then 'Medicaid HMO · 4 programs'\nSelected row is pale green"
process cue "On the right of the row\nWhat the payer asks for, read from its saved rules:\n'Initial + review', 'Initial only' or 'Review only'"
process prog "Programs\nA built-in payer covers every program that has a document list\nA payer added with 'Add a payer' covers the programs chosen then\n'4 programs' when all four, else the names"
decision dot "Does this payer have a change waiting?"
process green "Green dot, nothing else\nLabel for screen readers: 'No change waiting'"
process ochre "Ochre dot with the words 'Change waiting'"
toast tnote "A proposal from Historian alone\ndoes not mark the row.\nOnly the 'Changes' tab badge counts it"
process nomet "No approval rate or decision time on the row\nThose figures live in Analytics"

input i1 "Type in 'Search payers'"
process filt "List narrows as you type\nMatches name, plan type or group,\nany capitals"
decision any "Does any payer still match?"
toast empty "No payer matches 'text you typed'."
click clr "Click 'Clear search'"
process clr2 "Search box empties\nEvery payer shows again"

click pick "Click a payer row"
process nav "Address becomes /payers/the-payer?tab=\nSame tab as before. Process if none"
process swap "Header, tab bar and tab content\nswitch to the new payer"
process fresh "Tab content starts fresh\nNo editor, search text or result carries over"
process keep "Search text in the list stays"
click same "Click the payer that is already selected"
process nochg "Nothing changes on screen"
end e1 "The chosen payer's page is showing"

s1 --> list --> grp --> row --> cue --> prog --> dot
dot -->|No| green --> nomet
dot -->|Yes| ochre --> nomet
ochre -.-> tnote
list --> i1 --> filt --> any
any -->|No| empty --> clr --> clr2 --> list
any -->|Yes| pick
list --> pick
pick --> nav --> swap --> fresh --> keep --> e1
list --> same --> nochg --> e1
